# export {};
# -- end of source
# `holder.bump();`: some of the receivers have a row in the table of methods and the others have none: a test of the shape, the call through the table on one side, the read and the call as written on the other.
# The other side guesses at the method that it finds and has a meeting of its own, and what nobody reads behind a meeting is bound to nothing. The walk took "nothing is bound" for "this side has ended":
# the block of that meeting, which two edges lead to, had no end: the build stopped.
# f2 = turn
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = CallTable {{*}}key="bump"
# CHECK: = PropGet {{*}}key="bump"
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=f
# CHECK: = Call {{*}}calleeKey="bump"
